              "segment": {
                "start_index": null,
                "end_index": 209,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "When the BICEP2 (Background Imaging of Cosmic Extragalactic Polarization) collaboration announced its findings in March 2014, the physics and astronomy communities were pushed into a state of absolute euphoria"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                2
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 211,
                "end_index": 289,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Prominent physicists suggested it was a surefire Nobel Prize-winning discovery"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                3
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 211,
                "end_index": 366,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Prominent physicists suggested it was a surefire Nobel Prize-winning discovery, and some even compared its significance to the discovery of the Higgs boson"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                2,
                4
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 598,
                "end_index": 815,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "It Was the \"Smoking Gun\" for Cosmic Inflation\nIn 1980, physicist Alan Guth proposed the theory of **cosmic inflation** to solve major puzzles in cosmology (such as why the universe looks so uniform in every direction)"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                5,
                4
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 817,
                "end_index": 1068,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "The theory posits that in the first fraction of a microsecond after the Big Bang (around $10^{-36}$ seconds), the universe underwent an unimaginably violent, exponential expansion, ballooning by a factor of at least $10^{25}$ in a mere blink of an eye"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                5,
                6
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1156,
                "end_index": 1238,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "BICEP2 claimed to have found the first **direct evidence** of this rapid expansion"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                7,
                5
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1248,
                "end_index": 1469,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Detection of Primordial Gravitational Waves\nAccording to theory, the violent stretching of space-time during inflation would have generated massive ripples in the fabric of the universe: **primordial gravitational waves**"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                7,
                5
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1473,
                "end_index": 1761,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "As these waves rippled through the infant universe, they would have squeezed and stretched space, imprinting a very specific, faint, swirling polarization pattern\u2014known as **B-mode polarization**\u2014onto the Cosmic Microwave Background (CMB), the fossil light left over from the Big Bang"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                7,
                8,
                9
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1763,
                "end_index": 1856,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "BICEP2's telescope at the South Pole was designed to look for these exact \"swirls\" in the sky"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                6
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1858,
                "end_index": 1945,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Finding them was akin to finding the physical \"fingerprints\" of the birth of space-time"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                2,
                10
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1955,
                "end_index": 2175,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "A Bridge to Quantum Gravity\nOne of the greatest challenges in modern physics is unifying **General Relativity** (Einstein's theory of gravity and the very large) with **Quantum Mechanics** (the physics of the very small)"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                5,
                4
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 2179,
                "end_index": 2333,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Primordial gravitational waves are believed to have originated as tiny, subatomic *quantum fluctuations* that were stretched to cosmic scales by inflation"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                4,
                10
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 2335,
                "end_index": 2500,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "If BICEP2 had actually detected these waves, it would have been the first-ever observational proof that gravity is quantized (meaning it behaves under quantum rules)"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                0
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 2614,
                "end_index": 2750,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Looking Back to $10^{-36}$ Seconds After the Big Bang\nWhen we look at the universe using traditional light (even the CMB), we hit a wall"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                0,
                4
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 2752,
                "end_index": 2889,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "The CMB was emitted about 380,000 years after the Big Bang; before that, the universe was a hot, dense plasma that light could not escape"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                6
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 2893,
                "end_index": 2951,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Gravitational waves, however, do not get blocked by plasma"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                4,
                6
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 2953,
                "end_index": 3127,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Detecting primordial gravitational waves meant scientists could effectively look \"past\" the 380,000-year barrier, straight back to $10^{-36}$ seconds after the universe began"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                5
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 3129,
                "end_index": 3202,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "It was a telescope that could peer almost to the very instant of creation"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                7,
                11,
                0
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 3437,
                "end_index": 3691,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "By early 2015, a joint analysis between the BICEP2 team and the European Space Agency's **Planck satellite** team revealed a heartbreaking truth: the \"swirling\" B-mode polarization pattern BICEP2 detected wasn't from primordial gravitational waves at all"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                11,
                1
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 3693,
                "end_index": 3766,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Instead, it was caused by **cosmic dust** within our own Milky Way galaxy"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                11,
                1
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 3768,
                "end_index": 3906,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "The dust grains, aligned by galactic magnetic fields, scattered light in a way that perfectly mimicked the signature of the early universe"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                11
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 3909,
                "end_index": 4019,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "While the BICEP2 \"discovery\" turned out to be a false alarm, the experiment itself was a technological triumph"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                1,
                8
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 4146,
                "end_index": 4350,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Today, the hunt for primordial gravitational waves continues with next-generation experiments (like the BICEP Array and CMB-S4), as finding them remains one of the ultimate holy grails of modern cosmology"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            }
          ],
